---
import Main from "../../layouts/Main.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import LogoGrid from "../../components/LogoGrid.astro";
import {
  advisors,
  universityCollaborations,
  universityAssociations,
  communities,
} from "../../data/advisors";
import { BAN_ABOUT } from "../../data/media";
---

<Main
  title="Network - SyncI&DLabs"
  description="SyncI&DLabs pioneered the owner-operator venture-studio model before the form existed. Founder Francis Wang and a network of advisors and university collaborators, reading Canada's innovation ecosystems and actualizing the opportunities they reveal."
  lang="en"
  activePath="/network"
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Network"
    title="Ecosystem amplifiers who actualize."
    lead="We understand how Canada's innovation ecosystems work, where they leak value, and where the opportunities are. We pioneered the model that amplifies them. The district is the vehicle."
    image={BAN_ABOUT}
    imageAlt="Canadian research landscape at warm daylight"
  />

  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
      <div class="space-y-7 text-lg leading-relaxed text-graphite">
        <p>
          SyncI&DLabs, Synchronous Incubation and Development Labs, has run an owner-operator
          venture-studio model since 2013, before that form factor had a name. We were the novel
          inventors and pioneers of this methodology: not passive investors, not a service shop,
          but operators who build and turn around ventures from the inside and amplify the
          ecosystem around them.
        </p>
        <p>
          We have spent a decade inside the Canadian innovation gap. We know why founders leave,
          why IP is lost, and why districts fail when they treat land as the product. Our claim is
          different: opportunity analysis is credible because the people are inside the ecosystems
          they analyse. Francis Wang is the connective node; the network gives the reach.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The founding thesis: Waterloo -> Canada -->
  <section class="border-t border-hairline">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
      <p class="eyebrow text-graphite/60">The thesis, from Waterloo to Canada</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-6 max-w-4xl text-3xl font-medium leading-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        We saw a small place of vast potential. <br/>Now we see a country.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-graphite">
        In 2013, Waterloo looked like a town of outsized potential, and the question was how much
        of it you could help build by participating at the right time, with the right people. The
        answer, across the following decade, runs to an estimated 25 to 40 billion dollars. The
        same question now applies at national scale: Canada is a multi-trillion-dollar opportunity
        over the coming decades, if it can keep the value it creates.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-2 gap-8 md:grid-cols-4">
        <div>
          <div class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl" style="color: var(--wk-accent);">
            $25-40B
          </div>
          <div class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium text-graphite">
            Waterloo innovation value, 2013 to 2024 (estimated)
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl" style="color: var(--wk-accent);">
            $3-5T
          </div>
          <div class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium text-graphite">
            Canada's potential over 15 years, sovereignty scenario
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl" style="color: var(--wk-accent);">
            2013
          </div>
          <div class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium text-graphite">
            Pioneering the venture-studio model
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl" style="color: var(--wk-accent);">
            10
          </div>
          <div class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium text-graphite">
            University associations in the network
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-sm italic text-graphite/70">
        Regional and national figures are directional estimates under a coordinated
        sovereignty scenario, not verified forecasts. The verified problem statement is on
        <a href="/en/research" class="accent-link">The Canadian Gap</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Founder: connective node -->
  <section class="border-t border-hairline">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl items-start gap-12 px-6 py-20 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:px-10">
      <img
        src="/images/francis_wang.jpg"
        alt="Francis Wang, founder of SyncI&DLabs"
        width="640"
        height="800"
        loading="lazy"
        class="w-full border border-hairline object-cover"
        style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;"
      />
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow text-graphite/60">Founder</p>
        <h2 class="font-display mt-6 text-3xl font-medium leading-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
          Francis Wang
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-graphite">
          Founder of SyncI&DLabs and the connective node of the network. Owner-operator and
          venture-studio pioneer, doctoral researcher in CITAble and Hybrid Intelligence, and the
          originator of the actualizer method.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-graphite">
          Waterloo embeddedness runs through the work: Think Tank Labs at the Research and
          Technology Park, mentorship under Larry Smith, and an alumni network that still grounds
          opportunity reading in the region. Doctoral research spans the University of Waterloo,
          the University of Calgary, and Golden Gate University, with venture outcomes at the $70M
          and $650M scale behind the claim.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 10 university associations -->
  <section class="border-t border-hairline">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
      <p class="eyebrow text-graphite/60">University associations</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-6 max-w-3xl text-3xl font-medium leading-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        Reach across ten universities.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-graphite">
        The network spans ten universities as alma maters, doctoral homes, and collaboration
        partners. The breadth of that reach is the point: a network across the ecosystems the
        district draws on.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-12">
        <LogoGrid items={universityAssociations} captions={true} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Advisory board -->
  <section class="border-t border-hairline">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
      <p class="eyebrow text-graphite/60">Advisory board</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-6 max-w-3xl text-3xl font-medium leading-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        Advisors positioned by ecosystem embeddedness.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-graphite">
        Authority is human and networked. Each advisor is listed for where they sit inside an
        ecosystem, not for decorative prestige.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-px bg-hairline md:grid-cols-2">
        {
          advisors.map((a) => (
            <div class="bg-canvas p-9">
              <p class="eyebrow text-graphite/60">{a.role}</p>
              <h3 class="font-display mt-4 text-2xl font-medium text-ink">{a.name}</h3>
              <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-graphite">{a.embeddedness}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- University collaborations -->
  <section class="border-t border-hairline">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
      <p class="eyebrow text-graphite/60">University collaborations</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-6 max-w-3xl text-3xl font-medium leading-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        Collaborators, by practice.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-graphite">
        Beyond the advisory board, we engage a research-and-practice community across many
        institutions, each on a specific angle of practice.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-px bg-hairline sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {
          universityCollaborations.map((c) => (
            <div class="bg-canvas p-8">
              <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-medium text-ink">{c.university}</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink">{c.contact}</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-graphite">{c.angle}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Communities logo grid -->
  <section class="border-t border-hairline">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
      <p class="eyebrow text-graphite/60">Communities and institutes we engage</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-6 max-w-3xl text-3xl font-medium leading-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        Embedded across foresight, design, and practice communities.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-graphite">
        Association marks are nominative. They name the communities we engage; they are not
        endorsements.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-12">
        <LogoGrid items={communities} captions={true} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Main>
